3. Important S3 Security Concepts

IAM Policy

An identity-based policy that defines what an IAM user, group, or role can do.

Bucket Policy

A resource-based policy attached directly to an S3 bucket that controls access to the bucket and its resources.

Block Public Access

A security control that helps prevent unwanted public access to S3 data.

ACL

A traditional mechanism for controlling basic access permissions for S3 buckets and objects.

Encryption

Protects data stored in S3 by encrypting it at rest.

Versioning

Keeps multiple versions of an object and can help with recovery from accidental changes or deletions.

